      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_64be8966",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: immigrants_vs_illegal_aliens_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows a diverse group of people, many holding American flags, labeled 'immigrants,' implying they are welcomed or integrated members of society. The bottom image shows children and adults walking across a desert near a border fence, labeled 'illegal aliens,' implying they are unauthorized and undesirable. The intent is to create a false dichotomy by equating all immigrants with 'illegal aliens,' which is a harmful and inaccurate stereotype. This is hateful because it dehumanizes and vilifies a specific group (immigrants) by associating them with criminality and illegality, and it promotes xenophobic and anti-immigrant sentiment by implying that all immigrants are 'illegal aliens' — a term that is legally and morally loaded. The meme uses visual contrast to reinforce a prejudiced narrative that conflates legal immigration with illegal immigration, which is a form of hate speech targeting immigrants and promoting discriminatory attitudes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_86f82242"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
